    tag: 'v0.2.44',
    version: '0.2.44',
    name: null,
    body: '## What\'s Changed\n\n### 🚀 Features\n- **Improved web tool with explicit fetch/search modes** — The web tool now uses a discriminated union (`mode: "fetch"` / `mode: "search"`) instead of heuristic URL detection. Fetch mode works with any public URL; search mode explicitly targets the organization\'s knowledge base. The tool description now clearly communicates what each mode does and when to use it. (#1551)\n- **Citation header for web fetch results** — Fetch mode now returns a structured citation header and citations array, consistent with search mode output. (#1551)\n- **Better no-results guidance in web search** — When search returns no results, the agent now lists the organization\'s indexed websites so the user knows what\'s available and can take action (rephrase query, switch to fetch mode, or add a website). (#1551)\n\n### ⚡ Performance\n- **Increased similarity threshold for search relevance** — Default similarity threshold raised from 0.4 to 0.51 across RAG and web search, reducing low-quality results. (#1551)\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- **Context builder no longer drops user messages** — The structured context builder now accepts an explicit `promptMessageId` to skip only the exact message being sent as the LLM prompt. Previously it always skipped the last user message, which could drop context when the prompt was a system message (e.g. location response). (#1551)\n\n## Upgrade\n\nRun `tale upgrade` then `tale deploy` to update to this version.\n\nNo manual migration required.\n\n## Contributors\n@larryro\n\n---\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/tale-project/tale/compare/v0.2.43...v0.2.44',
